            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous coronary rotational atherectomy: New Jersey experience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complex coronary lesions can be approached percutaneously with rotational atherectomy. The first 70 procedures were performed at Newark Beth Israel Medical Center with a success rate of 94 percent. Despite treating a high-risk patient population, the complication rate was low.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
